{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "d3f1a9a0-1c2b-4a7e-9f0a-pixous-qa-collection",
    "name": "Pixous Technologies API \u2014 QA Collection",
    "description": "Synthetic-data QA collection for the Pixous Estimation & Invoicing API.\n\nSetup:\n1. Import the companion environment `Pixous_QA.postman_environment.json` and select it.\n2. Fill in `admin_password` (your local ADMIN_PASSWORD or a real Admin account password) and `qa_api_key` (must match QA_TEST_API_KEY in your .env - leave the QA API Key folder unused if you have not set one).\n3. Run 'Auth > Login (Admin)' first - it captures the JWT into the `jwt_token` environment variable, which every other request (except the QA API Key folder) uses automatically via Bearer auth.\n4. Run 'Estimations (Manual) > Create Manual Estimation' before the Invoices/Documents folders - it captures `base_name` into the environment for the rest of the chain.\n5. Run 'Jobs (AI Pipeline) > Create Job (Text)' before polling/wait/document requests in that folder - it captures `job_id`. Note: this hits the real LLM pipeline (Mistral/Groq/Gemini) if your .env has live API keys configured; it is not mocked here the way the automated pytest suite mocks it.\n\nAll request bodies use fictional/synthetic company and project data - no real client, financial, or personal information is included in this collection.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (Admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Bootstrap/admin login. Captures the returned JWT into {{jwt_token}} for every other request.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{admin_username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{admin_password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Login succeeded\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.environment.set(\"jwt_token\", body.token);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/validate",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "validate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public endpoint - always returns {status: valid}, does not itself check the token.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Public Branding",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/auth/branding",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "branding"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Unauthenticated - used by the login page to show the company logo before sign-in.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "QA API Key (alternate auth)",
      "description": "Demonstrates authenticating with X-API-Key instead of a Bearer token - for Postman/JMeter/k6 test runs where scripting a login flow first is inconvenient. Requires QA_TEST_API_KEY to be set in the server's .env (empty/unset in production disables this entirely). The key resolves to config.QA_TEST_USERNAME's role, so role-gated endpoints behave identically to a real login - this is a testing convenience, not an authorization bypass.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get Organization (via API Key)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-API-Key",
                "value": "{{qa_api_key}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/organization",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "organization"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same endpoint as the Bearer-token version, authenticated via the QA static key instead.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200 when QA_TEST_API_KEY is configured server-side\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect([200, 401]).to.include(pm.response.code);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
